S. court, and all three companies are industry leaders in the global memory semiconductor market."}, {"name": "~(으)면서 (while / simultaneous action)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Simultaneous-action marker. Two actions happen at once by the same subject: ''합의하다'' (agree) and ''유지하다'' (maintain prices) occur together.", "ex_ko": "원고 측은 세 회사가 서로 합의하면서 메모리 가격을 인위적으로 높게 유지했다고 주장합니다.", "ex_en": "The plaintiffs claim that the three companies colluded to keep memory prices artificially high."}, {"name": "~게 (adverbializer)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Forms adverb from adjective. 높다 (high) → 높게 (highly). Here: 가격을 높게 유지 = ''maintain prices high''.", "ex_ko": "원고 측은 세 회사가 서로 합의하면서 메모리 가격을 인위적으로 높게 유지했다고 주장합니다.", "ex_en": "The plaintiffs claim that the three companies colluded to keep memory prices artificially high."}, {"name": "~적으로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Adverb form of ~적 words: ''in a ~ way''. 인위적 (artificial) → 인위적으로 (artificially).", "ex_ko": "원고 측은 세 회사가 서로 합의하면서 메모리 가격을 인위적으로 높게 유지했다고 주장합니다.", "ex_en": "The plaintiffs claim that the three companies colluded to keep memory prices artificially high."}, {"name": "~다고 주장하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports a claim: ''claim that ~''. 유지했다 → 유지했다고 주장합니다 (claim that they kept).", "ex_ko": "원고 측은 세 회사가 서로 합의하면서 메모리 가격을 인위적으로 높게 유지했다고 주장합니다.", "ex_en": "The plaintiffs claim that the three companies colluded to keep memory prices artificially high."}, {"name": "~(으)로 인해/인한 (due to; causation)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Causation marker. 이 (this collusion) + 로 인해 = ''due to / as a result of''. Links cause (price fixing) to effect (overpayment).", "ex_ko": "이로 인해 소비자와 기업들이 정상 가격보다 더 높은 비용을 지불했다는 것이 소송의 핵심 내용입니다.", "ex_en": "The core claim of the lawsuit is that as a result, consumers and companies paid higher costs than normal prices."}, {"name": "~과/와 (and; listing)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Formal listing conjunction. Connects two noun phrases: 소비자 (consumers) and 기업들 (companies) as joint subjects.", "ex_ko": "이로 인해 소비자와 기업들이 정상 가격보다 더 높은 비용을 지불했다는 것이 소송의 핵심 내용입니다.", "ex_en": "The core claim of the lawsuit is that as a result, consumers and companies paid higher costs than normal prices."}, {"name": "~보다 (comparison: than)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Comparative particle. 정상 가격보다 = ''than normal prices''. Marks the reference point for comparison.", "ex_ko": "이로 인해 소비자와 기업들이 정상 가격보다 더 높은 비용을 지불했다는 것이 소송의 핵심 내용입니다.", "ex_en": "The core claim of the lawsuit is that as a result, consumers and companies paid higher costs than normal prices."}, {"name": "~았/었다는 것", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns a reported statement into a noun: ''the fact that ~''. 지불했다 → 지불했다는 것 (that they paid).", "ex_ko": "이로 인해 소비자와 기업들이 정상 가격보다 더 높은 비용을 지불했다는 것이 소송의 핵심 내용입니다.", "ex_en": "The core claim of the lawsuit is that as a result, consumers and companies paid higher costs than normal prices."}, {"name": "~을/를 토대로 (on the basis of)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Foundation/grounds marker. 혐의를 토대로 = ''on the basis of / grounded in allegations''. Indicates what the lawsuit is built upon.", "ex_ko": "이번 소송은 반독점법 위반 혐의를 토대로 제기되었습니다.", "ex_en": "This lawsuit was filed on the basis of allegations of antitrust law violations."}, {"name": "~았/었/였습니다 (past formal)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense formal-polite. 제기하다 (passive: 되다) + 었습니다 = ''was filed''.", "ex_ko": "이번 소송은 반독점법 위반 혐의를 토대로 제기되었습니다.", "ex_en": "This lawsuit was filed on the basis of allegations of antitrust law violations."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mqzust21bazm' and md5(translation) = 'e298c8ff12f784509374a50a1d62de0b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Keychron is a company that makes keyboards.", "The company got its start on Kickstarter in 2017.", "It now sells several types of keyboards, including the K2 model and one with an all-wood body."], "sentences": [{"text": "키크론은 키보드를 만드는 회사예요.", "translation": "Keychron is a company that makes keyboards.", "vocab": [{"ko": "키크론", "en": "Keychron (brand name)"}, {"ko": "키보드", "en": "keyboard"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make"}, {"ko": "회사", "en": "company"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Marks the topic of the sentence. 키크론 ends in a consonant, so 은: 키크론은 (as for Keychron).", "example_in_sentence": "키크론은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~를 (object particle)", "exp": "Marks the direct object of an action verb.", "example_in_sentence": "키보드를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (relative clause modifier)", "exp": "Modifies the following noun; present participle meaning ''that makes/which makes''.", "example_in_sentence": "만드는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요 (copula present)", "exp": "Present tense copula; states what something is. Informal polite form of 이다.", "example_in_sentence": "회사예요"}]}, {"text": "이 회사는 2017년에 킥스타터에서 시작했어요.", "translation": "This company started on Kickstarter in 2017.", "vocab": [{"ko": "회사", "en": "company"}, {"ko": "킥스타터", "en": "Kickstarter (platform name)"}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to start"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "이 (demonstrative determiner)", "exp": "Marks a specific noun as near to speaker; ''this''.", "example_in_sentence": "이 회사는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (time)", "exp": "Marks a point in time. 2017년 + 에 = 2017년에 (in 2017).", "example_in_sentence": "2017년에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (locative particle)", "exp": "Marks the place where an action happens or originates from.", "example_in_sentence": "킥스타터에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completion of past action; 시작하다 → 시작했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "시작했어요"}]}, {"text": "지금은 여러 종류의 키보드를 팔아요.", "translation": "Now it sells various types of keyboards.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금", "en": "now"}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "various; several"}, {"ko": "종류", "en": "type; kind"}, {"ko": "팔다", "en": "to sell"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic / contrast)", "exp": "Topic marker; here it contrasts now with the past. 지금 ends in a consonant, so 은: 지금은 (now).", "example_in_sentence": "지금은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive/genitive particle)", "exp": "Marks relationship between nouns; ''of'' or genitive modifier.", "example_in_sentence": "종류의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~를 (object particle)", "exp": "Marks the direct object of an action verb.", "example_in_sentence": "키보드를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present tense)", "exp": "Marks current or habitual action; 팔다 → 팔아요.", "example_in_sentence": "팔아요"}]}, {"text": "K2 모델도 있고, 나무로 만든 키보드도 있어요.", "translation": "There is a K2 model, and there are keyboards made of wood too.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모델", "en": "model"}, {"ko": "나무", "en": "wood"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (additive particle)", "exp": "Marks inclusion or addition; ''also'', ''too''.", "example_in_sentence": "모델도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinating conjunctive ending)", "exp": "Connects two clauses or predicates of equal status; lists items.", "example_in_sentence": "있고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~로 (instrumental particle)", "exp": "Marks the material or means; ''made of'' or ''with''.", "example_in_sentence": "나무로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 만들다 → 만든 키보드 (keyboards made ...); the ㄹ drops before ㄴ.", "example_in_sentence": "만든"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "exp": "Polite present ending. 있다 → 있어요 (there is / there are).", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "키크론", "en": "Keychron (brand name)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "키보드", "en": "keyboard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make", "note": ""}, {"ko": "회사", "en": "company", "note": ""}, {"ko": "킥스타터", "en": "Kickstarter (platform name)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to start", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "various; several", "note": ""}, {"ko": "종류", "en": "type; kind", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팔다", "en": "to sell", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모델", "en": "model", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나무", "en": "wood", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to have", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~은/는 (topic / contrast)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Topic marker; here it contrasts now with the past. 지금 ends in a consonant, so 은: 지금은 (now).", "ex_ko": "키크론은 키보드를 만드는 회사예요.", "ex_en": "Keychron is a company that makes keyboards."}, {"name": "~를 (object particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the direct object of an action verb.", "ex_ko": "키크론은 키보드를 만드는 회사예요.", "ex_en": "Keychron is a company that makes keyboards."}, {"name": "~는 (relative clause modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Modifies the following noun; present participle meaning ''that makes/which makes''.", "ex_ko": "키크론은 키보드를 만드는 회사예요.", "ex_en": "Keychron is a company that makes keyboards."}, {"name": "~예요 (copula present)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Present tense copula; states what something is. Informal polite form of 이다.", "ex_ko": "키크론은 키보드를 만드는 회사예요.", "ex_en": "Keychron is a company that makes keyboards."}, {"name": "이 (demonstrative determiner)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks a specific noun as near to speaker; ''this''.", "ex_ko": "이 회사는 2017년에 킥스타터에서 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "This company started on Kickstarter in 2017."}, {"name": "~에서 (locative particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the place where an action happens or originates from.", "ex_ko": "이 회사는 2017년에 킥스타터에서 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "This company started on Kickstarter in 2017."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks completion of past action; 시작하다 → 시작했어요.", "ex_ko": "이 회사는 2017년에 킥스타터에서 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "This company started on Kickstarter in 2017."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive/genitive particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks relationship between nouns; ''of'' or genitive modifier.", "ex_ko": "지금은 여러 종류의 키보드를 팔아요.", "ex_en": "Now it sells various types of keyboards."}, {"name": "~아/어요 (present polite)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Polite present ending. 있다 → 있어요 (there is / there are).", "ex_ko": "지금은 여러 종류의 키보드를 팔아요.", "ex_en": "Now it sells various types of keyboards."}, {"name": "~도 (additive particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks inclusion or addition; ''also'', ''too''.", "ex_ko": "K2 모델도 있고, 나무로 만든 키보드도 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a K2 model, and there are keyboards made of wood too."}, {"name": "~고 (coordinating conjunctive ending)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Connects two clauses or predicates of equal status; lists items.", "ex_ko": "K2 모델도 있고, 나무로 만든 키보드도 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a K2 model, and there are keyboards made of wood too."}, {"name": "~로 (instrumental particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the material or means; ''made of'' or ''with''.", "ex_ko": "K2 모델도 있고, 나무로 만든 키보드도 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a K2 model, and there are keyboards made of wood too."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Lets a past action describe a noun. 만들다 → 만든 키보드 (keyboards made ...); the ㄹ drops before ㄴ.", "ex_ko": "K2 모델도 있고, 나무로 만든 키보드도 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a K2 model, and there are keyboards made of wood too."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mv2csyyoaeqr' and md5(translation) = '5d3aa62c11c99497bec47ee0ff192764';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Five baby cheetahs were born on October 5, 2025, at the Smithsonian''s Conservation Biology Institute in Front Royal, Virginia, USA.", "The cubs'' mother is named Zura. She is five years old and takes good care of her babies.", "Baby cheetahs are born with their eyes closed, opening them after about four to seven days, and their ears are initially flat against their heads.", "The cubs gain about 50 grams of weight each day, and at six weeks old they will have their first veterinary exam.", "Cheetahs are the fastest land animals in the world, but their global population has dropped by more than 90 percent since 1900.", "The institute works to raise cheetahs in good health, and a total of 90 cheetahs have now been born at the facility."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국 버지니아주 스미스소니언 생물 보전 연구소에서 아기 치타 다섯 마리가 태어났어요.", "translation": "Five baby cheetahs were born at the Smithsonian Conservation Biology Institute in Virginia, USA.", "vocab": [{"ko": "치타", "en": "cheetah"}, {"ko": "태어나다", "en": "to be born"}, {"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals"}, {"ko": "연구소", "en": "research center"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle indicating the place/location where an action occurs. 연구소 (research center) + ~에서 marks where the babies were born.", "example_in_sentence": "연구소에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 태어나다 (to be born) becomes 태어났어요, indicating completed action in the past.", "example_in_sentence": "태어났어요"}]}, {"text": "태어난 날은 2025년 10월 5일이에요.", "translation": "The day they were born was October 5, 2025.", "vocab": [{"ko": "태어나다", "en": "to be born"}, {"ko": "날", "en": "day"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는", "exp": "Topic-marking particle. 날 (day) + ~은 marks the topic being introduced in the sentence.", "example_in_sentence": "날은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "이에요", "exp": "Present tense copula. Connects the subject to a predicate noun, equivalent to ''is''.", "example_in_sentence": "이에요"}]}, {"text": "아기 치타들의 엄마 이름은 주라예요.", "translation": "The mother cheetah''s name is Jura.", "vocab": [{"ko": "엄마", "en": "mother"}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle. 치타들 (baby cheetahs) + ~의 shows possession, creating ''the baby cheetahs'' mother''.", "example_in_sentence": "치타들의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "이에요/예요", "exp": "Polite ''is''. After a vowel, 이에요 becomes 예요: 주라 + 예요 = 주라예요 ''is Jura''.", "example_in_sentence": "주라예요"}]}, {"text": "주라는 다섯 살이에요.", "translation": "Jura is five years old.", "vocab": [{"ko": "살", "en": "years old"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Topic-marking particle. 주라 (proper noun) + ~는 marks the subject being discussed.", "example_in_sentence": "주라는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "이에요", "exp": "Present tense copula. Connects subject to age predicate.", "example_in_sentence": "이에요"}]}, {"text": "주라는 아기들을 잘 돌봐 줘요.", "translation": "Jura takes good care of the babies.", "vocab": [{"ko": "돌보다", "en": "to care for; to look after"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Direct object marker. 아기들 (babies) + ~을 marks the target of the action ''care for''.", "example_in_sentence": "아기들을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 주다", "exp": "Auxiliary construction expressing ''do something for someone''. 돌보다 becomes 돌봐, then + 주다, implying care done on behalf of others.", "example_in_sentence": "돌봐 줘요"}]}, {"text": "아기 치타들은 처음에 눈을 감고 태어나요.", "translation": "Baby cheetahs are born with their eyes closed at first.", "vocab": [{"ko": "처음", "en": "at first; initially"}, {"ko": "눈", "en": "eye"}, {"ko": "감다", "en": "to close"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Direct object marker. 눈 (eyes) + ~을 marks the target of the action ''close''.", "example_in_sentence": "눈을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective suffix indicating sequential or accompanying actions. 감다 becomes 감고, combining ''closing eyes'' with ''being born''.", "example_in_sentence": "감고"}]}, {"text": "4일에서 7일쯤 지나면 눈을 떠요.", "translation": "After about 4 to 7 days, they open their eyes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일", "en": "day"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass; to elapse"}, {"ko": "뜨다", "en": "to open"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Range marker in temporal expressions. 4일 to 7일 + ~에서 indicates a time range of 4-7 days.", "example_in_sentence": "4일에서 7일쯤"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Ending meaning ''if / when''. 지나다 → 지나면 ''when (the days) pass''.", "example_in_sentence": "지나면"}]}, {"text": "귀도 처음에는 머리에 붙어 있어요.", "translation": "At first, their ears are also attached to the head.", "vocab": [{"ko": "귀", "en": "ear"}, {"ko": "머리", "en": "head"}, {"ko": "붙다", "en": "to be attached"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also''. 귀 (ears) + ~도 indicates ears are mentioned in addition to eyes.", "example_in_sentence": "귀도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Locative particle. 머리 (head) + ~에 marks where ears are attached/located.", "example_in_sentence": "머리에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어 있다", "exp": "State/continuative aspect. 붙다 becomes 붙어 있어요, indicating a state of being attached.", "example_in_sentence": "붙어 있어요"}]}, {"text": "아기 치타들은 매일 약 50그램씩 무거워져요.", "translation": "The baby cheetahs get about 50 grams heavier every day.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매일", "en": "every day"}, {"ko": "약", "en": "about; approximately"}, {"ko": "무겁다", "en": "to be heavy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~씩", "exp": "Distribution/unit marker. 50그램 (50 grams) + ~씩 indicates the amount per each day.", "example_in_sentence": "50그램씩"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어지다", "exp": "Change of state suffix. 무겁다 becomes 무거워져요, indicating they become heavier (gradual change).", "example_in_sentence": "무거워져요"}]}, {"text": "여섯 주가 지나면 첫 번째 병원 검사를 받아요.", "translation": "After six weeks pass, they receive their first veterinary checkup.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주", "en": "week"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass"}, {"ko": "검사", "en": "checkup; examination"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~가", "exp": "Subject marker. 여섯 주 (six weeks) + ~가 marks the subject that does the action of passing.", "example_in_sentence": "주가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Ending meaning ''if / when''. 지나다 → 지나면 ''when (six weeks) pass''.", "example_in_sentence": "지나면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Direct object marker. 검사 (checkup) + ~를 marks the object being received.", "example_in_sentence": "검사를"}]}, {"text": "치타는 세계에서 가장 빠른 땅 위 동물이에요.", "translation": "The cheetah is the fastest land animal in the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세계", "en": "world"}, {"ko": "빠르다", "en": "to be fast"}, {"ko": "땅", "en": "land; ground"}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative/scope particle. 세계 (world) + ~에서 marks the scope within which the superlative applies.", "example_in_sentence": "세계에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "가장", "exp": "Superlative adverb meaning ''most''. Modifies 빠른 (fast) to create the superlative ''fastest''.", "example_in_sentence": "가장 빠른"}]}, {"text": "지금 치타는 수가 많이 줄었어요.", "translation": "Currently, the cheetah population has decreased significantly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금", "en": "now; currently"}, {"ko": "수", "en": "number; quantity"}, {"ko": "줄다", "en": "to decrease; to reduce"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Subject marker. 수 (number/quantity) + ~가 marks the subject of the sentence.", "example_in_sentence": "수가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 줄다 becomes 줄었어요, indicating a completed action in the past.", "example_in_sentence": "줄었어요"}]}, {"text": "1900년보다 90퍼센트 넘게 줄었어요.", "translation": "It has decreased by over 90 percent compared to 1900.", "vocab": [{"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~보다", "exp": "Comparative particle. 1900년 (the year 1900) + ~보다 marks the comparison point.", "example_in_sentence": "1900년보다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "Adverbial suffix. 넘다 becomes 넘게, functioning as an adverb modifying 줄었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "넘게"}]}, {"text": "이 연구소에서는 치타를 건강하게 키워요.", "translation": "This research center raises cheetahs healthily.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연구소", "en": "research center"}, {"ko": "건강하다", "en": "to be healthy"}, {"ko": "키우다", "en": "to raise; to bring up"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서는", "exp": "Locative + topic particle. 연구소 + ~에서는 marks the location as the topic of discussion.", "example_in_sentence": "연구소에서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Direct object marker. 치타 (cheetah) + ~를 marks the object being raised.", "example_in_sentence": "치타를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "Adverbial suffix. 건강하다 becomes 건강하게, modifying 키워요 to mean ''raise in a healthy manner''.", "example_in_sentence": "건강하게"}]}, {"text": "지금까지 이 연구소에서 치타 90마리가 태어났어요.", "translation": "So far, 90 cheetahs have been born at this research center.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금까지", "en": "so far; up to now"}, {"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals"}, {"ko": "태어나다", "en": "to be born"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지", "exp": "Extent/limit particle. 지금 + ~까지 creates ''up to now'', indicating a duration from past to present.", "example_in_sentence": "지금까지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Subject marker. 치타 90마리 (90 cheetahs) + ~가 marks the subject of the action.", "example_in_sentence": "마리가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix. 태어나다 becomes 태어났어요, indicating completed action from past to now.", "example_in_sentence": "태어났어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "치타", "en": "cheetah", "note": ""}, {"ko": "태어나다", "en": "to be born", "note": ""}, 