"아기 치타들은 처음에 눈을 감고 태어나요.", "ex_en": "Baby cheetahs are born with their eyes closed at first."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Ending meaning ''if / when''. 지나다 → 지나면 ''when (six weeks) pass''.", "ex_ko": "4일에서 7일쯤 지나면 눈을 떠요.", "ex_en": "After about 4 to 7 days, they open their eyes."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also''. 귀 (ears) + ~도 indicates ears are mentioned in addition to eyes.", "ex_ko": "귀도 처음에는 머리에 붙어 있어요.", "ex_en": "At first, their ears are also attached to the head."}, {"name": "~어 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "State/continuative aspect. 붙다 becomes 붙어 있어요, indicating a state of being attached.", "ex_ko": "귀도 처음에는 머리에 붙어 있어요.", "ex_en": "At first, their ears are also attached to the head."}, {"name": "~씩", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Distribution/unit marker. 50그램 (50 grams) + ~씩 indicates the amount per each day.", "ex_ko": "아기 치타들은 매일 약 50그램씩 무거워져요.", "ex_en": "The baby cheetahs get about 50 grams heavier every day."}, {"name": "~어지다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Change of state suffix. 무겁다 becomes 무거워져요, indicating they become heavier (gradual change).", "ex_ko": "아기 치타들은 매일 약 50그램씩 무거워져요.", "ex_en": "The baby cheetahs get about 50 grams heavier every day."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mv2d28mo2ha3' and md5(translation) = 'a593082eb85f184eccd9b87226fc0751';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["22-year-old Joy is an airplane pilot. Joy sat in the cockpit together with her dad on a KLM airplane.", "Joy''s dad Michel has worked as a pilot for 35 years. Joy liked her dad''s work since she was little.", "Joy''s mom Marianne also worked on the same airplane. Mom helped passengers inside the airplane.", "The three people didn''t know at first that they would work on the same airplane. Joy felt this experience was really special.", "Joy''s parents first met inside an airplane. Joy entered KLM flight school at age 17. So far she has flown together with her dad five times and with her mom once."], "sentences": [{"text": "22살 조이는 비행기 조종사예요.", "translation": "22-year-old Joy is an airplane pilot.", "vocab": [{"ko": "조종사", "en": "pilot", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking the subject as the main topic of the sentence. 조이 (Joy) + 는 = ''Joy (the topic) is...''", "example_in_sentence": "조이는"}]}, {"text": "조이는 KLM 비행기에서 아빠와 함께 조종석에 앉았어요.", "translation": "Joy sat in the cockpit together with her dad on a KLM airplane.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앉다", "en": "to sit", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking Joy as the main topic. 조이 + 는 = ''Joy (speaking of Joy)...''", "example_in_sentence": "조이는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (action-location)", "exp": "Marks the location where a dynamic action occurs. 비행기 + 에서 = ''on/in the airplane (where the sitting happens)''. Requires an action verb, not a state verb.", "example_in_sentence": "비행기에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~와/과 (with)", "exp": "Means ''with''. 와 follows a vowel (과 after a consonant): 아빠 + 와 = ''with dad''. 함께 ''together'' often follows.", "example_in_sentence": "아빠와"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location)", "exp": "Marks the specific location or destination where the action is directed. 조종석 + 에 = ''in/into the cockpit''. Here it indicates the destination of the sitting action.", "example_in_sentence": "조종석에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 앉다 (stem 앉-) + 았어요 = 앉았어요 ''sat''. Vowel ㅏ in stem triggers ~았.", "example_in_sentence": "앉았어요"}]}, {"text": "조이의 아빠 미셸은 35년 동안 조종사로 일했어요.", "translation": "Joy''s dad Michel has worked as a pilot for 35 years.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일하다", "en": "to work", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Possessive/relational genitive marker. 조이 + 의 = ''Joy''s'' (possession). 아빠 = ''dad''.", "example_in_sentence": "조이의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking Michel (아빠 미셸) as the main topic. 은 is used after consonant 셸.", "example_in_sentence": "미셸은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "Marks a role or capacity: 조종사 + 로 = ''as a pilot''.", "example_in_sentence": "조종사로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 일하다 → 일했어요 ''worked''.", "example_in_sentence": "일했어요"}]}, {"text": "조이는 어릴 때부터 아빠의 일을 좋아했어요.", "translation": "Joy liked her dad''s work since she was little.", "vocab": [{"ko": "좋아하다", "en": "to like", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking Joy as the topic. 조이 + 는 = ''Joy (as for Joy)...''", "example_in_sentence": "조이는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~부터 (from — starting point)", "exp": "Marks the starting point in time or sequence. 어릴 때 (when young) + 부터 = ''from/since the time she was young''.", "example_in_sentence": "때부터"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Possessive genitive marker. 아빠 + 의 + 일 = ''dad''s work''.", "example_in_sentence": "아빠의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 일 (work, consonant) + 을 = ''work'' as the direct object of 좋아하다 (to like).", "example_in_sentence": "일을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 좋아하다 → 좋아했어요 ''liked''.", "example_in_sentence": "좋아했어요"}]}, {"text": "조이의 엄마 마리얀도 같은 비행기에서 일했어요.", "translation": "Joy''s mom Marianne also worked on the same airplane.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일하다", "en": "to work", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Possessive genitive marker. 조이 + 의 + 엄마 = ''Joy''s mom''.", "example_in_sentence": "조이의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a noun modifier: 같다 ''to be the same'' → 같은 비행기 ''the same airplane''.", "example_in_sentence": "같은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also — additive)", "exp": "Inclusive particle meaning ''also/too''. 엄마 + 도 = ''mom too/also''. Adds Marianne to the list of people who worked on the airplane.", "example_in_sentence": "마리얀도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (action-location)", "exp": "Location where dynamic action occurs. 비행기 + 에서 = ''on/in the airplane'' (where she worked). Action verb 일하다 confirms dynamic action.", "example_in_sentence": "비행기에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 일하다 → 일했어요 ''worked''.", "example_in_sentence": "일했어요"}]}, {"text": "엄마는 비행기 안에서 손님들을 도왔어요.", "translation": "Mom helped passengers inside the airplane.", "vocab": [{"ko": "돕다", "en": "to help", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking mom as the topic. 엄마 + 는 = ''mom (as for mom)...''", "example_in_sentence": "엄마는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (action-location)", "exp": "Location where a dynamic action occurs. 비행기 안 (inside airplane) + 에서 = ''inside the airplane'' where helping happens.", "example_in_sentence": "안에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 손님들 (passengers, consonant) + 을 = ''passengers'' as the direct object of 돕다 (to help).", "example_in_sentence": "손님들을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅂ 불규칙 (ㅂ irregular)", "exp": "돕다 is ㅂ-irregular: the ㅂ changes to 오 before 아, so 돕다 → 도와 → 도왔어요 ''helped''.", "example_in_sentence": "도왔어요"}]}, {"text": "세 사람은 처음에 같은 비행기에서 일할 줄 몰랐어요.", "translation": "The three people didn''t know at first that they would work on the same airplane.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모르다", "en": "to not know", "note": "모르다 = not to know"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking the three people as topic. 사람 (consonant) + 은 = ''the three people (as for them)...''", "example_in_sentence": "사람은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a noun modifier: 같다 ''to be the same'' → 같은 비행기 ''the same airplane''.", "example_in_sentence": "같은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (action-location)", "exp": "Location of a dynamic action. 비행기 + 에서 = ''on/in the airplane'' (where the working would happen).", "example_in_sentence": "비행기에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 줄 몰랐다", "exp": "''Didn''t know that (something) would happen.'' 일하다 → 일할 줄 몰랐어요 ''didn''t know they would work''.", "example_in_sentence": "일할 줄 몰랐어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "르 불규칙 (르 irregular)", "exp": "모르다 is 르-irregular: before 아 it becomes 몰라, so the past form is 몰랐어요 ''didn''t know''.", "example_in_sentence": "몰랐어요"}]}, {"text": "조이는 이 경험이 정말 특별하게 느껴졌어요.", "translation": "Joy felt this experience was really special.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경험", "en": "experience", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "느껴지다", "en": "to feel; to be felt", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking Joy as the topic. 조이 + 는 = ''Joy...''", "example_in_sentence": "조이는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle marking the experience as the grammatical subject. 경험 (consonant) + 이 = ''this experience (which) felt special'' — the felt thing.", "example_in_sentence": "경험이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 (adverbializer)", "exp": "Forms adverbs from adjectives. 특별하다 (special) + 게 → 특별하게 ''specially/in a special way''. Modifies how the experience felt.", "example_in_sentence": "특별하게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite. 느껴지다 (to be felt) + 었어요 = 느껴졌어요 ''was felt/felt''. Vowel ㅓ triggers ~었.", "example_in_sentence": "느껴졌어요"}]}, {"text": "조이의 부모님은 비행기 안에서 처음 만났어요.", "translation": "Joy''s parents first met inside an airplane.", "vocab": [{"ko": "부모님", "en": "parents", "note": "honorific form of 부모"}, {"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의 (possessive)", "exp": "Possessive genitive. 조이 + 의 + 부모님 = ''Joy''s parents''.", "example_in_sentence": "조이의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. 부모님 (consonant) + 은 = ''the parents (as for them)...''", "example_in_sentence": "부모님은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (action-location)", "exp": "Location of a dynamic action. 비행기 안 (inside airplane) + 에서 = ''inside the airplane (where they met)''.", "example_in_sentence": "안에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite. 만나다 (to meet, stem 만나-) + 았어요 = 만났어요 ''met''. Vowel ㅏ triggers ~았.", "example_in_sentence": "만났어요"}]}, {"text": "조이는 17살에 KLM 비행 학교에 들어갔어요.", "translation": "Joy entered KLM flight school at age 17.", "vocab": [{"ko": "들어가다", "en": "to enter / to go in", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle marking Joy as topic. 조이 + 는 = ''Joy...''", "example_in_sentence": "조이는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (time point)", "exp": "Marks a point in time. 17살 (age 17) + 에 = ''at age 17''. Specifies when the entry happened.", "example_in_sentence": "17살에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (destination)", "exp": "Marks the destination or target of motion. 학교 + 에 = ''into/to school''. Object of the action 들어가다.", "example_in_sentence": "학교에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 들어가다 → 들어갔어요 ''entered'' (가 + 았 shortens to 갔).", "example_in_sentence": "들어갔어요"}]}, {"text": "지금까지 아빠와 다섯 번, 엄마와 한 번 함께 비행했어요.", "translation": "So far she has flown together with her dad five times and with her mom once.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비행하다", "en": "to fly", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~와/과 (with)", "exp": "Means ''with''. 와 follows a vowel (과 after a consonant): 아빠 + 와 = ''with dad''.", "example_in_sentence": "아빠와"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~와/과 (with)", "exp": "Same ''with'' in the second part: 엄마 + 와 = ''with mom''.", "example_in_sentence": "엄마와"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지 (until / up to — endpoint)", "exp": "Marks the endpoint of a range or quantity. 지금 (now) + 까지 = ''until now / so far''. Indicates the span from past to present moment.", "example_in_sentence": "지금까지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었/였어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite ending. 하다 verbs become 했어요: 비행하다 → 비행했어요 ''flew''.", "example_in_sentence": "비행했어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "조종사", "en": "pilot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앉다", "en": "to sit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일하다", "en": "to work", "note": ""}, {"ko": "좋아하다", "en": "to like", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돕다", "en": "to help", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모르다", "en": "to not know", "note": "모르다 = not to know"}, {"ko": "경험", "en": "experience", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "느껴지다", "en": "to feel; to be felt", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부모님", "en": "parents", "note": "honorific form of 부모"}, {"ko": "만나다", "en": "to meet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "들어가다", "en": "to enter / to go in", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비행하다", "en": "to fly", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Topic particle ma