게 느껴졌어요.", "ex_en": "Joy felt this experience was really special."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mv2vv51ssml0' and md5(translation) = '9a8bb6b7764e42118d4c5a529fcf2d15';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Bora, formerly of SISTAR, appeared on the YouTube channel ''No Back Tak,'' where she talked about her dating style and breakup experience.", "Bora said, ''I tend to take good care of others, so people say I''m like a mom,'' but added that she also wants to be on the receiving end of care.", "Bora also spoke about her personality, saying she talks seriously about issues only when the same problem comes up several times.", "When asked about her hardest breakup, Bora shared that at 3 p.m. her boyfriend texted her saying he was going to do something, but by 5 p.m. she received a call saying they should break up.", "Bora revealed that her ex said he had been thinking about it beforehand but never said anything, and she expressed that he should have at least given a hint instead of simply saying ''live well.''"], "sentences": [{"text": "시스타 출신 보라가 유튜브 채널 ''노빽탁''에 나왔어요.", "translation": "Bora, from Sistar, appeared on the YouTube channel ''Nobbyeok Tak''.", "vocab": [{"ko": "출신", "en": "(originally) from; former member of"}, {"ko": "채널", "en": "channel"}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to appear; to come out"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "보라는 이 방송에서 자신의 연애 스타일과 이별 경험을 이야기했어요.", "translation": "On this broadcast, Bora talked about her dating style and breakup experiences.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방송", "en": "broadcast; program"}, {"ko": "연애", "en": "dating; romantic relationship"}, {"ko": "이별", "en": "breakup; parting"}, {"ko": "경험", "en": "experience"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative/contextual particle indicating the setting or location of an action. ''방송에서'' = on the broadcast.", "example_in_sentence": "방송에서"}]}, {"text": "보라는 \"저는 상대방을 잘 챙겨요.", "translation": "Bora said, \"I take good care of the other person.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상대방", "en": "the other person; partner"}, {"ko": "챙기다", "en": "to take care of; to look after"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그래서 사람들이 저를 엄마 같다고 해요\"라고 말했어요.", "translation": "So people say I''m like a mom,\" she said.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "so; therefore; that''s why"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people"}, {"ko": "엄마", "en": "mother; mom"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "N 같다", "exp": "''To be like N'': 엄마 같다 = ''is like a mom''.", "example_in_sentence": "엄마 같다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Reported speech construction. ''같다고 해요'' = ''say/tell that (it) is like''; reports what others say.", "example_in_sentence": "같다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 보라는 \"저도 사실 누군가에게 받고 싶어요\"라고 했어요.", "translation": "However, Bora said, \"Actually, I want to be on the receiving end from someone too.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but; however"}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "actually; in fact"}, {"ko": "누군가", "en": "someone; somebody"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to take"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게 (from)", "exp": "With 받다, 에게 marks the giver, ''from'': 누군가에게 받다 = ''receive from someone''.", "example_in_sentence": "누군가에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 싶다", "exp": "Desiderative expression meaning ''want to''. ''받고 싶어요'' = 받다(receive) + 고 싶어요(want to).", "example_in_sentence": "받고 싶어요"}]}, {"text": "보라는 또 자신의 성격에 대해서도 이야기했어요.", "translation": "Bora also talked about her personality.", "vocab": [{"ko": "또", "en": "also; moreover; again"}, {"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself; one''s own"}, {"ko": "성격", "en": "personality; character"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 대해(서)", "exp": "Postposition phrase meaning ''about; concerning; regarding''. Shows the topic of discussion.", "example_in_sentence": "성격에 대해서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Particle ''also; too''. ''대해서도'' adds emphasis that this is another topic discussed.", "example_in_sentence": "대해서도"}]}, {"text": "그는 \"같은 문제가 여러 번 생기면 그때 진지하게 이야기해요\"라고 말했어요.", "translation": "She said, \"If the same problem occurs multiple times, then I talk seriously about it.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same"}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "problem; issue"}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "several; multiple"}, {"ko": "번", "en": "time(s); occasion(s)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Ending meaning ''if / when''. 생기다 → 생기면 ''if (the same problem) comes up''.", "example_in_sentence": "생기면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "Adverbial ending forming an adverb from adjective. ''진지하게'' = 진지하다(serious) + 게 (in a serious manner).", "example_in_sentence": "진지하게"}]}, {"text": "가장 힘든 이별에 대한 질문도 있었어요.", "translation": "There was also a question about the most difficult breakup.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가장", "en": "most; the most"}, {"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be hard; to be difficult"}, {"ko": "질문", "en": "question; query"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a noun modifier. 힘들다 drops its ㄹ: 힘들다 → 힘든 이별 ''a hard breakup''.", "example_in_sentence": "힘든"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also''. ''질문도'' = there was also a question.", "example_in_sentence": "질문도"}]}, {"text": "보라는 오후 3시에 남자 친구에게 \"나 뭐 좀 하고 올게\"라는 연락을 받았어요.", "translation": "Bora received a message from her boyfriend at 3 PM saying \"I''ll do something and be back.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "오후", "en": "afternoon; PM"}, {"ko": "남자 친구", "en": "boyfriend"}, {"ko": "연락", "en": "contact; message; communication"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "Dative particle ''to; from''. ''친구에게'' marks the source of the message.", "example_in_sentence": "친구에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는 (quoted modifier)", "exp": "Short for 라고 하는: links a quote to a noun. \"…올게\"라는 연락 = ''a message saying \"…\"''.", "example_in_sentence": "라는 연락"}]}, {"text": "그런데 오후 5시에 \"우리 헤어져야 할 것 같아\"라는 전화를 받았어요.", "translation": "But at 5 PM, she received a phone call saying \"I think we should break up.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "그런데", "en": "but; however; yet"}, {"ko": "헤어지다", "en": "to break up; to separate; to part"}, {"ko": "전화", "en": "phone call; telephone"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Obligation/necessity marker meaning ''must; have to; should''. ''헤어져야 하다'' = must break up.", "example_in_sentence": "헤어져야"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 것 같다", "exp": "Conjecture/supposition meaning ''seems like; appears to''. ''할 것 같아'' = seems/appears to (need to break up).", "example_in_sentence": "할 것 같아"}]}, {"text": "보라는 남자 친구가 \"미리 생각하고 있었지만 말을 안 했다\"고 했다고 전했어요.", "translation": "Bora conveyed that her boyfriend said he had been thinking about it beforehand but didn''t tell her.", "vocab": [{"ko": "미리", "en": "beforehand; in advance; previously"}, {"ko": "생각하다", "en": "to think"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있었다", "exp": "Progressive past tense. ''생각하고 있었다'' = was thinking (ongoing action in past).", "example_in_sentence": "생각하고 있었지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "Conjunctive ending meaning ''but; although; yet''. Connects contrasting clauses.", "example_in_sentence": "있었지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다 (reported speech)", "exp": "Reports someone''s words. Here it is stacked: he said \"…안 했다\" (했다고), and Bora passed that on (전했어요).", "example_in_sentence": "했다고 전했어요"}]}, {"text": "보라는 \"그러면 적어도 힌트라도 줘야 해요.", "translation": "Bora said, \"Then you should at least give a hint.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그러면", "en": "then; in that case; if so"}, {"ko": "적어도", "en": "at least; at the minimum"}, {"ko": "힌트", "en": "hint; clue"}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~라도", "exp": "Particle meaning ''at least; even if only''. ''힌트라도'' = even just a hint.", "example_in_sentence": "힌트라도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "''Have to; should''. 주다 → 줘야 해요 ''should give''.", "example_in_sentence": "줘야 해요"}]}, {"text": "그냥 ''잘 살아''라는 식이었어요\"라고 말했어요.", "translation": "It was just like, ''Have a good life,''\" she said.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그냥", "en": "just; simply; merely"}, {"ko": "식", "en": "way; style; manner"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~라는 식", "exp": "Expression meaning ''in a manner/way of saying...''. Describes how something was said or done.", "example_in_sentence": "''잘 살아''라는 식"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. ''이었어요'' = 이다(be) + 었어요 (past polite).", "example_in_sentence": "이었어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "출신", "en": "(originally) from; former member of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "채널", "en": "channel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to appear; to come out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방송", "en": "broadcast; program", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연애", "en": "dating; romantic relationship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이별", "en": "breakup; parting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경험", "en": "experience", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상대방", "en": "the other person; partner", "note": ""}, {"ko": "챙기다", "en": "to take care of; to look after", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그래서", "en": "so; therefore; that''s why", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "엄마", "en": "mother; mom", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but; however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "actually; in fact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "누군가", "en": "someone; somebody", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to take", "note": ""}, {"ko": "또", "en": "also; moreover; again", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자신", "en": "oneself; one''s own", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성격", "en": "personality; character", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "problem; issue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여러", "en": "several; multiple", "note": ""}, {"ko": "번", "en": "time(s); occasion(s)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가장", "en": "most; the most", "note": ""}, {"ko": "힘들다", "en": "to be hard; to be difficult", "note": ""}, {"ko": "질문", "en": "question; query", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오후", "en": "afternoon; PM", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남자 친구", "en": "boyfriend", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연락", "en": "contact; message; communication", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그런데", "en": "but; however; yet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헤어지다", "en": "to break up; to separate; to part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전화", "en": "phone call; telephone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "미리", "en": "beforehand; in advance; previously", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생각하다", "en": "to think", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그러면", "en": "then; in that case; if so", "note": ""}, {"ko": "적어도", "en": "at least; at the minimum", "note": ""}, {"ko": "힌트", "en": "hint; clue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그냥", "en": "just; simply; merely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "식", "en": "way; style; manner", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Locative/contextual particle indicating the setting or location of an action. ''방송에서'' = on the broadcast.", "ex_ko": "보라는 이 방송에서 자신의 연애 스타일과 이별 경험을 이야기했어요.", "ex_en": "On this broadcast, Bora talked about her dating style and breakup experiences."}, {"name": "N 같다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "''To be like N'': 엄마 같다 = ''is like a mom''.", "ex_ko": "그래서 사람들이 저를 엄마 같다고 해요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "So people say I''m like a mom,\" she said."}, {"name": "~다고 하다 (reported speech)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports someone''s words. Here it is stacked: he said \"…안 했다\" (했다고), and Bora passed that on (전했어요).", "ex_ko": "그래서 사람들이 저를 엄마 같다고 해요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "So people say I''m like a mom,\" she said."}, {"name": "~에게 (from)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "With 받다, 에게 marks the giver, ''from'': 누군가에게 받다 = ''receive from someone''.", "ex_ko": "하지만 보라는 \"저도 사실 누군가에게 받고 싶어요\"라고 했어요.", "ex_en": "However, Bora said, \"Actually, I want to be on the receiving end from someone too.\""}, {"name": "~고 싶다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Desiderative expression meaning ''want to''. ''받고 싶어요'' = 받다(receive) + 고 싶어요(want to).", "ex_ko": "하지만 보라는 \"저도 사실 누군가에게 받고 싶어요\"라고 했어요.", "ex_en": "However, Bora said, \"Actually, I want to be on the receiving end from someone too.\""}, {"name": "~에 대해(서)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Postposition phrase meaning ''about; concerning; regarding''. Shows the topic of discussion.", "ex_ko": "보라는 또 자신의 성격에 대해서도 이야기했어요.", "ex_en": "Bora also talked about her personality."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Particle ''also; too''. ''대해서도'' adds emphasis that this is another topic discussed.", "ex_ko": "보라는 또 자신의 성격에 대해서도 이야기했어요.", "ex_en": "Bora also talked about her personality."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Ending meaning ''if / when''. 생기다 → 생기면 ''if (the same problem) comes up''.", "ex_ko": "그는 \"같은 문제가 여러 번 생기면 그때 진지하게 이야기해요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "She said, \"If the same problem occurs multiple times, then I talk seriously about it.\""}, {"name": "~게", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Adverbial ending forming an adverb from adjective. ''진지하게'' = 진지하다(serious) + 게 (in a serious manner).", "ex_ko": "그는 \"같은 문제가 여러 번 생기면 그때 진지하게 이야기해요\"라고 말했어요.", "ex_en": "She said, \"If the same problem occurs multiple times, then I talk seriously about it.\""}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Turns an adjective into a noun modifier. 힘들다 drops its ㄹ: 힘들다 → 힘든 이별 ''a hard breakup''.", "ex_ko": "가장 힘든 이별에 대한 질문도 있었어요.", "ex_en": "There was also a question about the most difficult breakup."}, {"name": "~(이)라는 (quoted modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Short for 라고 하는: links a quote to a noun. \"…올게\"라는 연락 = ''a message saying \"…\"''.", "ex_ko": "보라는 오후 3시에 남자 친구에게 \"나 뭐 좀 하고 올게\"라는 연락을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "Bora received a message from her boyfriend at 3 PM saying \"I''ll do something and be back.\""}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Obligation/necessity marker meaning ''must; have to; should''. ''헤어져야 하다'' = must break up.", "ex_ko": "그런데 오후 5시에 \"우리 헤어져야 할 것 같아\"라는 전화를 받았어요.", "ex_en": "But at 5 PM, she received a phone call saying \"I think we should break up.\""}, {"name": "~ㄹ 것 같다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Conjecture/supposition meaning ''seems like; appears to''. ''할 것 같아'' = seems/appears to (need to break up).", "ex_ko": "그런데 오후 5시에 \"우리 헤어져야 할 것 같아\"라는 전화를 받았어요.", "ex_en": "But at 5 PM, she received a phone call saying \"I think we should break up.\""}, {"name": "~고 있었다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive past tense. ''생각하고 있었다'' = was thinking (ongoing action in past).", "ex_ko": "보라는 남자 친구가 \"미리 생각하고 있었지만 말을 안 했다\"고 했다고 전했어요.", "ex_en": "Bora conveyed that her boyfriend said he had been thinking about it beforehand but didn''t tell her."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Conjunctive ending meaning ''but; although; yet''. Connects contrasting clauses.", "ex_ko": "보라는 남자 친구가 \"미리 생각하고 있었지만 말을 안 했다\"고 했다고 전했어요.", "ex_en": "Bora conveyed that her boyfriend said he had been thinking about it beforehand but didn''t tell her."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mv2w1oebmqjf' and md5(translation) = '8a666a8cc50936057595a335e465b315';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Canadian writer Anne Carson has been awarded the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature. As a poet, translator, classicist, essayist, and visual artist, she has expanded the boundaries of contemporary literature for over four decades.", "What stands out most in Carson''s work is not the originality of form, but her ability to make thought itself a literary event. By connecting scholarship and creative writing as one, she has demonstrated that intellectual writing and imagination can enrich each other.", "Carson is also well known for her deep exploration of ancient Greek literature. She regards ancient writers such as Sappho, Simonides, Sophocles, and Euripides not as mere objects of study but as conversational partners. In her writing, the voices of antiquity connect with the present through themes such as desire, sorrow, loss, and death.", "Her work repeatedly addresses the theme of distance: distance between lovers, distance between languages, and distance between the living and the dead. Carson portrays desire not as a movement toward possession but as an encounter with absence, finding both suffering and possibility in the gaps and intervals within human experience.", "This thematic consciousness is intimately connected with formal experimentation. In works such as \"Eros the Bittersweet,\" \"Autobiography of Red,\" \"Beauty of the Husband,\" \"Nox,\" and \"Float,\" she employs fragmentation, quotation, rupture, and collage techniques. These forms are not decoration but methods of inquiry.", "Carson''s influence is already evident among younger generations of writers and scholars. The growing number of those who move freely between criticism, translation, poetry, and prose has learned intellectual freedom from Carson''s approach to writing. The Nobel Prize in Literature has often recognized writers who have expanded the possibilities of literature, and Anne Carson is clearly one such writer."], "sentences": [{"text": "캐나다 작가 앤 카슨이 2026년 노벨 문학상을 받게 되었습니다.", "translation": "Canadian writer Anne Carson has been awarded the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature.", "vocab": [{"ko": "노벨 문학상", "en": "Nobel Prize in Literature"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Expresses a change of state or resultant condition; marks an unexpected or inevitable outcome. Chain: 받다 → 받게 되다.", "example_in_sentence": "받게 되었습니다"}]}, {"text": "그는 시인, 번역가, 고전학자, 수필가, 시각 예술가로 활동하면서 40년 이상 현대 문학의 경계를 넓혀 왔습니다.", "translation": "Working as a poet, translator, classicist, essayist and visual artist, she has been widening the boundaries of contemporary literature for over 40 years.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고전학자", "en": "classicist; classical scholar"}, {"ko": "수필가", "en": "essayist"}, {"ko": "경계를 넓히다", "en": "expand boundaries; broaden horizons"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "''While (doing)'': two things happen at the same time. 활동하다 → 활동하면서 ''while working (as)''.", "example_in_sentence": "활동하면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 왔다", "exp": "Auxiliary verb construction marking a continuous action from past to present. Chain: 넓히다 → 넓혀 왔다.", "example_in_sentence": "넓혀 왔습니다"}]}, {"text": "카슨의 작품에서 가장 주목할 점은 형식의 독창성보다는 사유 자체를 문학적 사건으로 만드는 능력입니다.", "translation": "The most noteworthy point in Carson''s works is the ability to make thought itself into a literary event, rather than the originality of form.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주목하다", "en": "pay attention to; notice"}, {"ko": "독창성", "en": "originality; uniqueness"}, {"ko": "사유", "en": "thought; reflection; thinking"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 점", "exp": "A prospective modifier + 점 ''point'': 주목하다 → 주목할 점 ''a point worth noting''.", "example_in_sentence": "주목할 점"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~보다는", "exp": "Contrastive particle marking preference or shift of focus; indicates ''rather than'' or ''instead of''. Compares two entities.", "example_in_sentence": "독창성보다는"}]}, {"text": "학문과 창작을 하나로 연결하면서 지적인 글쓰기와 상상력이 서로를 풍요롭게 할 수 있다는 것을 보여 주었습니다.", "translation": "By connecting scholarship and creative work as one, she demonstrated that intellectual writing and imagination can mutually enrich each other.", "vocab": [{"ko": "학문", "en": "scholarship; learning; academics"}, {"ko": "풍요롭게 하다", "en": "enrich; make abundant"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "''Can; be able to''. 하다 → 할 수 있다 ''can (enrich)''.", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 있다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 것", "exp": "Turns a whole statement into a noun, ''the fact that…'': 할 수 있다 → 할 수 있다는 것을 보여 주다 ''show that (they) can…''.", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 있다는 것을"}]}, {"text": "카슨은 고대 그리스 문학을 깊이 탐구하는 것으로도 잘 알려져 있습니다.", "translation": "Carson is also well known for deeply exploring ancient Greek literature.", "vocab": [{"ko": "탐구하다", "en": "explore; investigate; probe"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것으로", "exp": "Nominalizing suffix + instrumental particle; marks the means or basis for which something is known. Chain: 탐구하다 → 탐구하는 것으로.", "example_in_sentence": "탐구하는 것으로도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다 (state)", "exp": "Shows a resulting state: 알려지다 ''to become known'' → 알려져 있다 ''is known''.", "example_in_sentence": "알려져 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "사포, 시모니데스, 소포클레스, 에우리피데스 같은 고대 작가들을 단순한 연구 대상이 아니라 대화 상대로 여기기 때문입니다.", "translation": "Because she regards ancient writers such as Sappho, Simonides, Sophocles, and Euripides not as mere objects of study but as conversation partners.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여기다", "en": "regard; view; consider"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~이 아니라", "exp": "Contrastive negation particle; marks explicit rejection of one thing in favor of another. Negates and introduces alternative.", "example_in_sentence": "대상이 아니라"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Causal nominalizing suffix; marks the reason or cause. Chain: 여기다 → 여기기 때문이다.", "example_in_sentence": "여기기 때문입니다"}]}, {"text": "그의 글 속에서 고대의 목소리는 욕망, 슬픔, 상실, 죽음 같은 주제를 통해 현재와 연결됩니다.", "translation": "In her writing, ancient voices connect with the present through themes such as desire, sorrow, loss and death.", "vocab": [{"ko": "목소리", "en": "voice; sound"}, {"ko": "상실", "en": "loss; deprivation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을 통해", "exp": "Particle marking means or medium; ''through'' or ''by means of''. Indicates channel of connection.", "example_in_sentence": "주제를 통해"}]}, {"text": "그의 작품은 거리라는 주제를 반복해서 다룹니다.", "translation": "Her works return again and again to the theme of distance.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거리", "en": "distance; gap; space"}, {"ko": "다루다", "en": "deal with; handle; treat"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "Links a name or label to a noun, ''called / of'': 거리라는 주제 ''the theme of distance''.", "example_in_sentence": "거리라는 주제"}]}, {"text": "연인 사이의 거리, 언어와 언어 사이의 거리, 산 자와 죽은 자 사이의 거리가 그것입니다.", "translation": "They are the distance between lovers, the distance between languages, and the distance between the living and the dead.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연인", "en": "lover; beloved; sweetheart"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "카슨은 욕망을 소유를 향한 움직임이 아니라 부재와의 만남으로 그려 내며, 인간 경험 속의 틈과 간격에서 고통과 가능성을 동시에 찾아냅니다.", "translation": "Carson depicts desire not as movement toward possession but as an encounter with absence, and simultaneously finds suffering and possibility in the gaps and spaces within human experience.", "vocab": [{"ko": "욕망", "en": "desire; wanting; craving"}, {"ko": "소유", "en": "possession; ownership"}, {"ko": "부재", "en": "absence; non-presence"}, {"ko": "틈", "en": "gap; crack; fissure"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 향한", "exp": "Relative particle marking direction or aim; ''directed toward'' or ''aimed at''.", "example_in_sentence": "소유를 향한 움직임"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)며", "exp": "Connective suffix expressing multiple concurrent or sequential actions; and/while/at the same time. Chain: 그려내다 → 그려 내며.", "example_in_sentence": "그려 내며"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "N 속의", "exp": "속 ''inside'' + 의 links it to the next noun: 인간 경험 속의 틈 ''the gaps within human experience''.", "example_in_sentence": "경험 속의 틈"}]}, {"text": "이러한 주제 의식은 형식 실험과 긴밀하게 연결되어 있습니다.", "translation": "This thematic consciousness is closely connected to formal experimentation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주제 의식", "en": "thematic consciousness; awareness of theme"}, {"ko": "긴밀하다", "en": "close; tight; intimate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Auxiliary marking state or resultant condition of a completed action. Chain: 연결되다 → 연결되어 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "연결되어 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "『에로스, 쓴 달콤함』, 『붉음의 자서전』, 『남편의 아름다움』, 『녹스』, 『플로트』 등의 작품에서 단편화, 인용, 단절, 콜라주 기법을 사용합니다.", "translation": "In works such as ''Eros the Bittersweet'', ''Autobiography of Red'', ''Beauty of the Husband'', ''Nox'', and ''Float'', she employs fragmentation, quotation, disjunction, and collage techniques.", "vocab": [{"ko": "단편화", "en": "fragmentation; breaking into fragments"}, {"ko": "인용", "en": "quotation; citation"}, {"ko": "단절", "en": "disconnection; rupture; break"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이러한 형식은 장식이 아니라 탐구의 방식입니다.", "translation": "Such form is not decoration but a method of inquiry.", "vocab": [{"ko": "장식", "en": "decoration; ornament"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~이 아니라", "exp": "Contrastive negation; rejects first proposition and asserts second.", "example_in_sentence": "장식이 아니라"}]}, {"text": "카슨의 영향은 이미 젊은 세대의 작가들과 학자들에게서 나타나고 있습니다.", "translation": "Carson''s influence is already showing in writers and scholars of the younger generation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "영향", "en": "influence; impact; effect"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Auxiliary marking progressive or ongoing action. Chain: 나타나다 → 나타나고 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "나타나고 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "비평, 번역, 시, 산문 사이를 자유롭게 오가는 이들이 늘어난 것은 카슨의 작업 방식에서 지적 자유를 배웠기 때문입니다.", "translation": "The increase in those who freely move between criticism, translation, poetry, and prose is because they learned intellectual freedom from Carson''s working methods.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비평", "en": "criticism; critique"}, {"ko": "오가다", "en": "come and go; move back and forth; shuttle"}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "increase; grow; expand"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 이들", "exp": "Relative modifier + noun; marks those performing the action. Chain: 오가다 → 오가는 이들.", "example_in_sentence": "오가는 이들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Causal nominalizing suffix marking reason or cause for preceding clause.", "example_in_sentence": "배웠기 때문입니다"}]}, {"text": "노벨 문학상은 문학의 가능성을 확장한 작가들을 자주 인정해 왔는데, 앤 카슨은 분명 그 자리에 속하는 작가입니다.", "translation": "The Nobel Prize in Literature has frequently recognized writers who expanded literary possibilities, and Anne Carson is clearly a writer who belongs in that place.", "vocab": [{"ko": "확장하다", "en": "expand; extend; widen"}, {"ko": "인정하다", "en": "acknowledge; recognize; admit"}, {"ko": "속하다", "en": "belong to; be part of; fall into"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 왔다", "exp": "Auxiliary marking repeated or continuous action from past to present. Chain: 인정하다 → 인정해 왔다.", "example_in_sentence": "인정해 왔는데"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는데", "exp": "Connective ending marking contrast, background, or transition between clauses.", "example_in_sentence": "왔는데"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "노벨 문학상", "en": "Nobel Prize in Literature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고전학자", "en": "classicist; classical scholar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수필가", "en": "essayist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경계를 넓히다", "en": "expand boundaries; broaden horizons", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주목하다", "en": "pay attention to; notice", "note": ""}, {"ko": "독창성", "en": "originality; uniqueness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사유", "en": "thought; reflection; thinking", "note": ""}, {"ko": "학문", "en": "scholarship; learning; academics", "note": ""}, {"ko": "풍요롭게 하다", "en": "enrich; make abundant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "탐구하다", "en": "explore; investigate; probe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "여기다", "en": "regard; view; consider", "note": ""}, {"ko": "목소리", "en": "voice; sound", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상실", "en": "loss; deprivation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거리", "en": "distance; gap; space", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다루다", "en": "deal with; handle; treat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연인", "en": "lover; beloved; sweetheart", "note": ""}, {"ko": "욕망", "en": "desire; wanting; craving", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소유", "en": "possession; ownership", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부재", "en": "absence; non-presence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "틈", "en": "gap; crack; fissure", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주제 의식", "en": "thematic consciousness; awareness of theme", "note": ""}, {"ko": "긴밀하다", "en": "close; tight; intimate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단편화", "en": "fragmentation; breaking into fragments", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인용", "en": "quotation; citation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단절", "en": "disconnection; rupture; break", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장식", "en": "decoration; ornament", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "influence; impact; effect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비평", "en": "criticism; critique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오가다", "en": "come and go; move back and forth; shuttle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "increase; grow; expand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확장하다", "en": "expand; extend; widen", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인정하다", "en": "acknowledge; recognize; admit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "속하다", "en": "belong to; be part of; fall into", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경계", "en": "boundary; border; limit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넓혀 오다", "en": "have been expanding; have been broadening", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "be known; become known", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연결되다", "en": "be connected; be linked", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "method; manner; way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "appear; emerge; show", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Expresses a change of state or resultant condition; marks an unexpected or inevitable outcome. Chain: 받다 → 받게 되다.", "ex_ko": "캐나다 작가 앤 카슨이 2026년 노벨 문학상을 받게 되었습니다.", "ex_en": "Canadian writer Anne Carson has been awarded the 2026 Nobel Prize in Literature."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "''While (doing)'': two things happen at the same time. 활동하다 → 활동하면서 ''while working (as)''.", "ex_ko": "그는 시인, 번역가, 고전학자, 수필가, 시각 예술가로 활동하면서 40년 이상 현대 문학의 경계를 넓혀 왔습니다.", "ex_en": "Working as a poet, translator, classicist, essayist and visual artist, she has been widening the boundaries of contemporary literature for over 40 years."}, {"name": "~아/어 왔다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Auxiliary verb construction marking a continuous action from past to present. Chain: 넓히다 → 넓혀 왔다.", "ex_ko": "그는 시인, 번역가, 고전학자, 수필가, 시각 예술가로 활동하면서 40년 이상 현대 문학의 경계를 넓혀 왔습니다.", "ex_en": "Working as a poet, translator, classicist, essayist and visual artist, she has been widening the boundaries of contemporary literature for over 40 years."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 점", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "A prospective modifier + 점 ''point'': 주목하다 → 주목할 점 ''a point worth noting''.", "ex_ko": "카슨의 작품에서 가장 주목할 점은 형식의 독창성보다는 사유 자체를 문학적 사건으로 만드는 능력입니다.", "ex_en": "The most noteworthy point in Carson''s works is the ability to make thought itself into a literary event, rather than the originality of form."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "''Can; be able to''. 하다 → 할 수 있다 ''can (enrich)''.", "ex_ko": "학문과 창작을 하나로 연결하면서 지적인 글쓰기와 상상력이 서로를 풍요롭게 할 수 있다는 것을 보여 주었습니다.", "ex_en": "By connecting scholarship and creative work as one, she demonstrated that intellectual writing and imagination can mutually enrich each other."}, {"name": "~다는 것", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Turns a whole statement into a noun, ''the fact that…'': 할 수 있다 → 할 수 있다는 것을 보여 주다 ''show that (they) can…''.", "ex_ko": "학문과 창작을 하나로 연결하면서 지적인 글쓰기와 상상력이 서로를 풍요롭게 할 수 있다는 것을 보여 주었습니다.", "ex_en": "By connecting scholarship and creative work as one, she demonstrated that intellectual writing and imagination can mutually enrich each other."}, {"name": "~는 것으로", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Nominalizing suffix + instrumental particle; marks the means or basis for which something is known. Chain: 탐구하다 → 탐구하는 것으로.", "ex_ko": "카슨은 고대 그리스 문학을 깊이 탐구하는 것으로도 잘 알려져 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Carson is also well known for deeply exploring ancient Greek literature."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다 (state)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Auxiliary marking state or resultant condition of a completed action. Chain: 연결되다 → 연결되어 있다.", "ex_ko": "카슨은 고대 그리스 문학을 깊이 탐구하는 것으로도 잘 알려져 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Carson is also well known for deeply exploring ancient Greek literature."}, {"name": "~기 때문이다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Causal nominalizing suffix; marks the reason or cause. Chain: 여기다 → 여기기 때문이다.", "ex_ko": "사포, 시모니데스, 소포클레스, 에우리피데스 같은 고대 작가들을 단순한 연구 대상이 아니라 대화 상대로 여기기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "Because she regards ancient writers such as Sappho, Simonides, Sophocles, and Euripides not as mere objects of study but as conversation partners."}, {"name": "~을 통해", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Particle marking means or medium; ''through'' or ''by means of''. Indicates channel of connection.", "ex_ko": "그의 글 속에서 고대의 목소리는 욕망, 슬픔, 상실, 죽음 같은 주제를 통해 현재와 연결됩니다.", "ex_en": "In her writing, ancient voices connect with the present through themes such as desire, sorrow, loss and death."}, {"name": "~(이)라는", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Links a name or label to a noun, ''called / of'': 거리라는 주제 ''the theme of distance''.", "ex_ko": "그의 작품은 거리라는 주제를 반복해서 다룹니다.", "ex_en": "Her works return again and again to the theme of distance."}, {"name": "~(으)며", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Connective suffix expressing multiple concurrent or sequential actions; and/while/at the same time. Chain: 그려내다 → 그려 내며.", "ex_ko": "카슨은 욕망을 소유를 향한 움직임이 아니라 부재와의 만남으로 그려 내며, 인간 경험 속의 틈과 간격에서 고통과 가능성을 동시에 찾아냅니다.", "ex_en": "Carson depicts desire not as movement toward possession but as an encounter with absence, and simultaneously finds suffering and possibility in the gaps and spaces within human experience."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Auxiliary marking progressive or ongoing action. Chain: 나타나다 → 나타나고 있다.", "ex_ko": "카슨의 영향은 이미 젊은 세대의 작가들과 학자들에게서 나타나고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Carson''s influence is already showing in writers and scholars of the younger generation."}, {"name": "~는 이들", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Relative modifier + noun; marks those performing the action. Chain: 오가다 → 오가는 이들.", "ex_ko": "비평, 번역, 시, 산문 사이를 자유롭게 오가는 이들이 늘어난 것은 카슨의 작업 방식에서 지적 자유를 배웠기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "The increase in those who freely move between criticism, translation, poetry, and prose is because they learned intellectual freedom from Carson''s working methods."}, {"name": "~는데", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Connective ending marking contrast, background, or transition between clauses.", "ex_ko": "노벨 문학상은 문학의 가능성을 확장한 작가들을 자주 인정해 왔는데, 앤 카슨은 분명 그 자리에 속하는 작가입니다.", "ex_en": "The Nobel Prize in Literature has frequently recognized writers who expanded literary possibilities, and Anne Carson is clearly a writer who belongs in that place."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mv2w8e4ewpkw' and md5(translation) = '6b360b60151772ccef6a1e8bd411ed76';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Scientists at the Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory under the U.S. Department of Energy have proposed a new pathway that could require significantly less energy to achieve nuclear fusion ignition. Three physicists—Luis Delgado-Aparicio, Masayuki Ono, and Jonathan Menard—developed a new equation that extends the existing Lawson criterion and published their findings in the academic journal Physical Review Letters.", "To sustain a nuclear fusion reaction, plasma must maintain a sufficiently high temperature and density. The conventional approach followed the sequence of first raising the plasma density and then supplying heat. However, according to the research team''s calculations, reversing this order—heating the plasma first before increasing its density—could be considerably more efficient.", "Delgado-Aparicio compared this to a route through a mountain range. Whereas the conventional method attempts to cross the mountain peak head-on, the new approach is like taking a detour through a lower pass, he explained. The research team named the point corresponding to this detour the \"Kodeira saddle point\" and revealed that the ideal fusion output to external heating ratio required to pass through this point is approximately 5.", "In deriving the new criterion, the research team additionally incorporated four physical factors that had been omitted from existing models. Particularly noteworthy are the results related to tungsten contamination. Tungsten is a metal used for the inner walls of next-generation fusion devices and excels in heat resistance; however, even when its concentration in the plasma is only one ten-thousandth, it was found to approximately double the pressure required for ignition. When calculations were extended to three dimensions, it was also confirmed that the required pressure could potentially exceed the stability limit of the plasma.", "Meanwhile, it was also revealed that the energy loss that makes ignition difficult simultaneously provides a balancing effect that suppresses thermal runaway instability. The research team also proposed that coating the reactor wall with liquid lithium or utilizing spin-polarized fuel could help overcome these barriers. However, this research is a theoretical achievement based on mathematical calculations, and experimental verification has not yet been conducted."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국 에너지부 산하 프린스턴 플라즈마 물리연구소의 과학자들이 핵융합 점화를 달성하는 데 훨씬 적은 에너지가 소요될 수 있는 새로운 경로를 제시하기에 이르렀습니다.", "translation": "Scientists at Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory under the U.S. Department of Energy have come to present a new pathway by which much less energy could be required to achieve nuclear fusion ignition.", "vocab": [{"ko": "산하", "en": "under; subordinate to"}, {"ko": "점화", "en": "ignition"}, {"ko": "소요되다", "en": "to be required; to be needed"}, {"ko": "이르다", "en": "to reach; to come to"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 데", "exp": "''In / for doing (something)'': 달성하는 데 (에너지가) 소요되다 = ''(energy) is needed to achieve (ignition)''.", "example_in_sentence": "달성하는 데"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기에 이르다", "exp": "Auxiliary verb construction meaning ''to come to'' or ''to reach the point of.'' The ~기 nominalized form + 이르다 emphasizes progression to a significant state or event.", "example_in_sentence": "제시하기에 이르렀습니다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Modal construction expressing possibility. The prospective ~ㄹ + 수 (possibility) + 있다 indicates potential ability or likelihood.", "example_in_sentence": "소요될 수 있는"}]}, {"text": "루이스 델가도아파리시오, 오노 마사유키, 조너선 메너드 세 물리학자는 기존의 로손 기준을 확장한 새로운 수식을 개발하여 그 결과를 학술지 피지컬 리뷰 레터스에 발표하였습니다.", "translation": "Three physicists—Luis Delgado Aparicio, Masayuki Ono, and Jonathan Menard—developed a new formula that extended the existing Lawson criterion and published the results in the academic journal Physical Review Letters.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기존", "en": "existing; conventional"}, {"ko": "기준", "en": "criterion; standard"}, {"ko": "확장하다", "en": "to extend; to expand"}, {"ko": "발표하다", "en": "to publish; to announce"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 (-여)", "exp": "Formal written ''and then'': 개발하다 → 개발하여 ''developed (it), and…'' (= 개발해서).", "example_in_sentence": "개발하여"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past modifier on an action verb: 확장하다 → 확장한 수식 ''a formula that extended (the criterion)''.", "example_in_sentence": "확장한 새로운 수식"}]}, {"text": "핵융합 반응을 지속시키려면 플라즈마가 충분히 뜨겁고 밀도가 높은 상태를 유지하여야 합니다.", "translation": "To sustain nuclear fusion reaction, plasma must maintain a sufficiently hot and high-density state.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지속시키다", "en": "to sustain; to maintain"}, {"ko": "충분히", "en": "sufficiently; adequately"}, {"ko": "밀도", "en": "density"}, {"ko": "유지하다", "en": "to maintain; to keep"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~려면", "exp": "Conditional connective meaning ''in order to'' or ''if (one wants to).'' Expresses a prerequisite condition for the main clause.", "example_in_sentence": "지속시키려면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinating adjectives)", "exp": "Coordinator joining two descriptive predicates: 뜨겁고 (hot) and 높은 (high). Both modify the noun 상태 (state).", "example_in_sentence": "충분히 뜨겁고 밀도가 높은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Obligation/necessity construction. 유지하여야 합니다 means ''must maintain.'' The ~아/어야 morpheme marks obligation.", "example_in_sentence": "유지하여야 합니다"}]}, {"text": "기존의 접근 방식은 플라즈마의 밀도를 먼저 높인 뒤 열을 공급하는 순서를 따랐습니다.", "translation": "The conventional approach followed the order of first raising plasma density and then supplying heat.", "vocab": [{"ko": "접근", "en": "approach; access"}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "method; way"}, {"ko": "높이다", "en": "to raise; to increase"}, {"ko": "공급하다", "en": "to supply; to provide"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 뒤", "exp": "''After doing'': 높이다 → 높인 뒤 ''after raising (the density)''.", "example_in_sentence": "높인 뒤"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle modifier)", "exp": "Relative clause form modifying 순서 (order). 공급하는 means ''that supplies'' or ''of supplying.''", "example_in_sentence": "열을 공급하는 순서"}]}, {"text": "그러나 연구진의 계산에 의하면, 순서를 반대로 하여 밀도를 높이기 전에 플라즈마를 먼저 가열하는 방법이 훨씬 효율적일 수 있다고 합니다.", "translation": "However, according to the team''s calculations, reversing the order and heating the plasma first, before raising its density, could be far more efficient.", "vocab": [{"ko": "계산", "en": "calculation; computation"}, {"ko": "반대로", "en": "conversely; in reverse"}, {"ko": "가열하다", "en": "to heat; to warm"}, {"ko": "효율적", "en": "efficient"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에 의하면", "exp": "According to; on the basis of. Indicates the source of information or standard upon which a statement is based.", "example_in_sentence": "연구진의 계산에 의하면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 전에", "exp": "Temporal preposition meaning ''before.'' The ~기 nominalizer + 전에 indicates that action 1 occurs before action 2.", "example_in_sentence": "밀도를 높이기 전에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다고 하다", "exp": "Reports a claim of possibility: 효율적이다 → 효율적일 수 있다고 합니다 ''(they say it) could be efficient''.", "example_in_sentence": "효율적일 수 있다고 합니다"}]}, {"text": "델가도아파리시오는 이를 산맥을 통과하는 경로에 비유하였습니다.", "translation": "Delgado Aparicio compared it to a pathway passing through a mountain range.", "vocab": [{"ko": "산맥", "en": "mountain range"}, {"ko": "통과하다", "en": "to pass through; to cross"}, {"ko": "경로", "en": "path; route"}, {"ko": "비유하다", "en": "to compare; to liken"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle modifier)", "exp": "Relative clause modifying 경로 (pathway). 통과하는 means ''that passes through.''", "example_in_sentence": "산맥을 통과하는 경로"}]}, {"text": "기존 방식이 산 정상을 정면으로 넘으려는 것이라면, 새로운 방식은 더 낮은 고개를 통해 우회하는 것과 같다고 하였습니다.", "translation": "If the conventional method is like trying to climb straight over a mountain peak, the new method is like going around it through a lower pass, he said.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정상", "en": "peak; summit"}, {"ko": "정면", "en": "head-on; directly"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to cross; to go over"}, {"ko": "우회하다", "en": "to circumvent; to detour"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려는", "exp": "''Trying / intending to'' as a noun modifier: 넘다 → 넘으려는 것 ''an attempt to cross (head-on)''.", "example_in_sentence": "넘으려는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라면", "exp": "''If it is…'' after a noun: 것이다 → 것이라면 ''if (the old way) is…''.", "example_in_sentence": "것이라면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것과 같다", "exp": "Simile or comparison construction. Nominalizer ~는 것 + comparison marker 와/과 + 같다 (same/like).", "example_in_sentence": "우회하는 것과 같다고"}]}, {"text": "연구진은 이 우회로에 해당하는 지점을 ''코데이 안부''라고 명명하였으며, 이 지점을 통과하는 데 필요한 외부 가열 대비 융합 출력 비율은 이상적인 조건에서 약 5에 해당한다고 밝혔습니다.", "translation": "The team named the point on this detour the ''Cordey pass'' and said that, under ideal conditions, the ratio of fusion output to external heating needed to get through it is about 5.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해당하다", "en": "to correspond to; to apply to"}, {"ko": "명명하다", "en": "to name; to designate"}, {"ko": "대비", "en": "compared to; relative to"}, {"ko": "밝히다", "en": "to disclose; to reveal"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 데 필요한", "exp": "''Needed for doing'': 통과하다 → 통과하는 데 필요한 ''needed to pass through''.", "example_in_sentence": "통과하는 데 필요한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~으며 (sequential coordination)", "exp": "Connector joining two coordinate clauses of equal importance. 명명하였으며 + second clause. Shows both actions performed by the subject.", "example_in_sentence": "명명하였으며"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~라고 (direct quotation marker)", "exp": "Reports exact name or designation. Used with 명명하다 to mark what something is called.", "example_in_sentence": "''코데이 안부''라고 명명하였으며"}]}, {"text": "연구진은 새로운 기준을 도출하는 데 있어 기존 모델에서 누락되었던 네 가지 물리적 요인을 추가로 반영하였습니다.", "translation": "In deriving the new criterion, the research team additionally reflected four physical factors that had been omitted from the existing model.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도출하다", "en": "to derive; to deduce"}, {"ko": "누락되다", "en": "to be omitted; to be left out"}, {"ko": "요인", "en": "factor; element"}, {"ko": "반영하다", "en": "to reflect; to incorporate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~는 데 있어", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning ''in the process of'' or ''in (doing something).'' Marks the context or domain where an action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "기준을 도출하는 데 있어"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었던 (retrospective past participle)", "exp": "Past participle indicating a state that existed before the present moment. 누락되었던 means ''that had been omitted.''", "example_in_sentence": "누락되었던 네 가지 물리적 요인"}]}, {"text": "특히 텅스텐 오염과 관련한 결과는 주목할 만합니다.", "translation": "Particularly, results related to tungsten contamination are noteworthy.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly"}, {"ko": "텅스텐", "en": "tungsten"}, {"ko": "오염", "en": "contamination; pollution"}, {"ko": "주목하다", "en": "to pay attention to; to note"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~와/과 관련한", "exp": "''Related to N'': 오염과 관련한 결과 ''results related to contamination''.", "example_in_sentence": "텅스텐 오염과 관련한 결과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 만하다", "exp": "Sufficiency/worthiness construction meaning ''worth doing'' or ''deserving.'' Here 주목할 만하다 = ''worthy of attention.''", "example_in_sentence": "주목할 만합니다"}]}, {"text": "텅스텐은 차세대 핵융합 장치 내벽에 사용되는 금속인 만큼 내열성 면에서 우수하지만, 플라즈마 내 농도가 만 분의 일에 불과하더라도 점화에 필요한 압력을 약 두 배로 높이는 것으로 나타났습니다.", "translation": "As a metal used for the inner walls of next-generation fusion devices, tungsten has excellent heat resistance, but even at a concentration of just one ten-thousandth in the plasma, it was found to roughly double the pressure needed for ignition.", "vocab": [{"ko": "차세대", "en": "next generation"}, {"ko": "내벽", "en": "inner wall"}, {"ko": "내열성", "en": "heat resistance"}, {"ko": "우수하다", "en": "to be excellent; to be superior"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~인 만큼", "exp": "''As / since (it is)'': 금속이다 → 금속인 만큼 ''as it is a metal (used for…)''.", "example_in_sentence": "금속인 만큼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~더라도", "exp": "Ending meaning ''even if'': 불과하다 → 불과하더라도 ''even if it is only (one ten-thousandth)''.", "example_in_sentence": "불과하더라도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것으로 나타나다", "exp": "''Was shown to / turned out to'': 높이다 → 높이는 것으로 나타났습니다 ''was found to raise''.", "example_in_sentence": "높이는 것으로 나타났습니다"}]}, {"text": "계산을 3차원으로 확장하였을 때 필요 압력이 플라즈마 안정성의 한계를 초과할 가능성도 확인되었습니다.", "translation": "When the calculation was extended to three dimensions, the possibility that the required pressure would exceed the limit of plasma stability was also confirmed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "확장하다", "en": "to extend; to expand"}, {"ko": "한계", "en": "limit; boundary"}, {"ko": "초과하다", "en": "to exceed; to surpass"}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; potential"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/ㄹ 때", "exp": "Temporal adverbial meaning ''when.'' 확장하였을 때 = ''when the extension was done.'' Marks the time frame of the main action.", "example_in_sentence": "3차원으로 확장하였을 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/ㄹ 가능성", "exp": "Nominalization expressing ''possibility'' or ''likelihood.'' The prospective form ~을/ㄹ + 가능성.", "example_in_sentence": "초과할 가능성"}]}, {"text": "한편, 점화를 어렵게 만드는 에너지 손실이 열 폭주 불안정을 억제하는 균형 효과를 동시에 제공한다는 점도 밝혀졌습니다.", "translation": "Meanwhile, it was also revealed that energy loss that makes ignition difficult simultaneously provides a balancing effect that suppresses thermal runaway instability.", "vocab": [{"ko": "에너지 손실", "en": "energy loss"}, {"ko": "억제하다", "en": "to suppress; to inhibit"}, {"ko": "균형", "en": "balance; equilibrium"}, {"ko": "밝혀지다", "en": "to be revealed; to come to light"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (noun modifier)", "exp": "Present modifier on action verbs: 만들다 → 만드는 (ㄹ drops), 억제하다 → 억제하는. 어렵게 만드는 에너지 손실 ''energy loss that makes (ignition) hard''.", "example_in_sentence": "어렵게 만드는 에너지 손실"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~다는 점", "exp": "Nominalized reporting structure meaning ''the point that'' or ''the fact that.'' Used to emphasize a reported finding.", "example_in_sentence": "제공한다는 점도 밝혀졌습니다"}]}, {"text": "연구진은 또한 반응로 내벽에 액체 리튬을 코팅하거나 스핀 편극 연료를 활용하는 방법이 이러한 장벽을 극복하는 데 기여할 수 있다고 제안하였습니다.", "translation": "The research team also proposed that methods such as coating liquid lithium on the inner wall of the reactor or utilizing spin-polarized fuel could contribute to overcoming these barriers.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반응로", "en": "reactor"}, {"ko": "코팅하다", "en": "to coat"}, {"ko": "액체", "en": "liquid"}, {"ko": "극복하다", "en": "to overcome; to surmount"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~거나 (disjunctive coordination)", "exp": "Coordinator offering alternatives. 코팅하거나 스핀 편극 연료를 활용하는 = ''either coating or utilizing.'' Joins two alternative methods.", "example_in_sentence": "코팅하거나 스핀 편극 연료를 활용하는 방법"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~는 데 기여하다", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning ''to contribute to.'' The nominalizer ~는 데 + 기여하다.", "example_in_sentence": "극복하는 데 기여할 수 있다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다고 제안하다", "exp": "Reported potential. The embedded clause (possibility) is reported with ~다고 제안하다 (proposed that).", "example_in_sentence": "기여할 수 있다고 제안하였습니다"}]}, {"text": "다만 이번 연구는 수학적 계산에 기반한 이론적 성과로, 실험을 통한 검증은 아직 이루어지지 않았습니다.", "translation": "However, this research is a theoretical achievement based on mathematical calculations, and verification through experimentation has not yet been conducted.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다만", "en": "however; but"}, {"ko": "기반하다", "en": "to base; to ground"}, {"ko": "성과", "en": "achievement; result"}, {"ko": "검증", "en": "verification; validation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 기반한 (past participle modifier)", "exp": "Relative clause meaning ''based on.'' The past participle 기반한 modifies 성과 (achievement).", "example_in_sentence": "수학적 계산에 기반한 이론적 성과"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않았다", "exp": "Negative past ''has not (yet)'': 이루어지다 ''to be carried out'' → 이루어지지 않았습니다 ''has not been carried out''.", "example_in_sentence": "이루어지지 않았습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "산하", "en": "under; subordinate to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "점화", "en": "ignition", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소요되다", "en": "to be required; to be needed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이르다", "en": "to reach; to come to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기존", "en": "existing; conventional", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기준", "en": "criterion; standard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확장하다", "en": "to extend; to expand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발표하다", "en": "to publish; to announce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지속시키다", "en": "to sustain; to maintain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "충분히", "en": "sufficiently; adequately", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밀도", "en": "density", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유지하다", "en": "to maintain; to keep", "note": ""}, {"ko": "접근", "en": "approach; access", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "method; way", "note": ""}, {"ko": "높이다", "en": "to raise; to increase", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공급하다", "en": "to supply; to provide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계산", "en": "calculation; computation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반대로", "en": "conversely; in reverse", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가열하다", "en": "to heat; to warm", "note": ""}, {"ko": "효율적", "en": "efficient", "note": ""}, {"ko": "산맥", "en": "mountain range", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통과하다", "en": "to pass through; to cross", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경로", "en": "path; route", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비유하다", "en": "to compare; to liken", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정상", "en": "peak; summit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정면", "en": "head-on; directly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to cross; to go over", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우회하다", "en": "to circumvent; to detour", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해당하다", "en": "to correspond to; to apply to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "명명하다", "en": "to name; to designate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대비", "en": "compared to; relative to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밝히다", "en": "to disclose; to reveal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도출하다", "en": "to derive; to deduce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "누락되다", "en": "to be omitted; to be left out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "요인", "en": "factor; element", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반영하다", "en": "to reflect; to incorporate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "텅스텐", "en": "tungsten", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오염", "en": "contamination; pollution", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주목하다", "en": "to pay attention to; to note", "note": ""}, {"ko": "차세대", "en": "next generation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "내벽", "en": "inner wall", "note": ""}, {"ko": "내열성", "en": "heat resistance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우수하다", "en": "to be excellent; to be superior", "note": ""}, {"ko": "한계", "en": "limit; boundary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "초과하다", "en": "to exceed; to surpass", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; potential", "note": ""}, {"ko": "에너지 손실", "en": "energy loss", "note": ""}, {"ko": "억제하다", "en": "to suppress; to inhibit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "균형", "en": "balance; equilibrium", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밝혀지다", "en": "to be revealed; to come to light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반응로", "en": "reactor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "코팅하다", "en": "to coat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "액체", "en": "liquid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "극복하다", "en": "to overcome; to surmount", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다만", "en": "however; but", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기반하다", "en": "to base; to ground", "note": ""}, {"ko": "성과", "en": "achievement; result", "note": ""}, {"ko": "검증", "en": "verification; validation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수식", "en": "formula; equation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "학술지", "en": "academic journal; scholarly publication", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뜨겁다", "en": "to be hot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "열", "en": "heat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "순서", "en": "order; sequence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의하면", "en": "according to; based on", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관련하다", "en": "to be related to; to relate to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사용되다", "en": "to be used; to be utilized", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확인되다", "en": "to be confirmed; to be verified; to be ascertained", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어렵게 만들다", "en": "to make difficult; to cause difficulty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "손실", "en": "loss; wastage; leak", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to utilize; to use; to make use of", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 데", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "''In / for doing (something)'': 달성하는 데 (에너지가) 소요되다 = ''(energy) is needed to achieve (ignition)''.", "ex_ko": "미국 에너지부 산하 프린스턴 플라즈마 물리연구소의 과학자들이 핵융합 점화를 달성하는 데 훨씬 적은 에너지가 소요될 수 있는 새로운 경로를 제시하기에 이르렀습니다.", "ex_en": "Scientists at Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory under the U.S. Department of Energy have come to present a new pathway by which much less energy could be required to achieve nuclear fusion ignition."}, {"name": "~기에 이르다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Auxiliary verb construction meaning ''to come to'' or ''to reach the point of.'' The ~기 nominalized form + 이르다 emphasizes progression to a significant state or event.", "ex_ko": "미국 에너지부 산하 프린스턴 플라즈마 물리연구소의 과학자들이 핵융합 점화를 달성하는 데 훨씬 적은 에너지가 소요될 수 있는 새로운 경로를 제시하기에 이르렀습니다.", "ex_en": "Scientists at Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory under the U.S. Department of Energy have come to present a new pathway by which much less energy could be required to achieve nuclear fusion ignition."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Modal construction expressing possibility. The prospective ~ㄹ + 수 (possibility) + 있다 indicates potential ability or likelihood.", "ex_ko": "미국 에너지부 산하 프린스턴 플라즈마 물리연구소의 과학자들이 핵융합 점화를 달성하는 데 훨씬 적은 에너지가 소요될 수 있는 새로운 경로를 제시하기에 이르렀습니다.", "ex_en": "Scientists at Princeton Plasma Physics Laboratory under the U.S. Department of Energy have come to present a new pathway by which much less energy could be required to achieve nuclear fusion ignition."}, {"name": "~아/어 (-여)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Formal written ''and then'': 개발하다 → 개발하여 ''developed (it), and…'' (= 개발해서).", "ex_ko": "루이스 델가도아파리시오, 오노 마사유키, 조너선 메너드 세 물리학자는 기존의 로손 기준을 확장한 새로운 수식을 개발하여 그 결과를 학술지 피지컬 리뷰 레터스에 발표하였습니다.", "ex_en": "Three physicists—Luis Delgado Aparicio, Masayuki Ono, and Jonathan Menard—developed a new formula that extended the existing Lawson criterion and published the results in the academic journal Physical Review Letters."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Past modifier on an action verb: 확장하다 → 확장한 수식 ''a formula that extended (the criterion)''.", "ex_ko": "루이스 델가도아파리시오, 오노 마사유키, 조너선 메너드 세 물리학자는 기존의 로손 기준을 확장한 새로운 수식을 개발하여 그 결과를 학술지 피지컬 리뷰 레터스에 발표하였습니다.", "ex_en": "Three physicists—Luis Delgado Aparicio, Masayuki Ono, and Jonathan Menard—developed a new formula that extended the existing Lawson criterion and published the results in the academic journal Physical Review Letters."}, {"name": "~려면", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Conditional connective meaning ''in order to'' or ''if (one wants to).'' Expresses a prerequisite condition for the main clause.", "ex_ko": "핵융합 반응을 지속시키려면 플라즈마가 충분히 뜨겁고 밀도가 높은 상태를 유지하여야 합니다.", "ex_en": "To sustain nuclear fusion reaction, plasma must maintain a sufficiently hot and high-density state."}, {"name": "~고 (coordinating adjectives)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Coordinator joining two descriptive predicates: 뜨겁고 (hot) and 높은 (high). Both modify the noun 상태 (state).", "ex_ko": "핵융합 반응을 지속시키려면 플라즈마가 충분히 뜨겁고 밀도가 높은 상태를 유지하여야 합니다.", "ex_en": "To sustain nuclear fusion reaction, plasma must maintain a sufficiently hot and high-density state."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Obligation/necessity construction. 유지하여야 합니다 means ''must maintain.'' The ~아/어야 morpheme marks obligation.", "ex_ko": "핵융합 반응을 지속시키려면 플라즈마가 충분히 뜨겁고 밀도가 높은 상태를 유지하여야 합니다.", "ex_en": "To sustain nuclear fusion reaction, plasma must maintain a sufficiently hot and high-density state."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 뒤", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "''After doing'': 높이다 → 높인 뒤 ''after raising (the density)''.", "ex_ko": "기존의 접근 방식은 플라즈마의 밀도를 먼저 높인 뒤 열을 공급하는 순서를 따랐습니다.", "ex_en": "The conventional approach followed the order of first raising plasma density and then supplying heat."}, {"name": "~는 (present participle modifier)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Present modifier on action verbs: 만들다 → 만드는 (ㄹ drops), 억제하다 → 억제하는. 어렵게 만드는 에너지 손실 ''energy loss that makes (ignition) hard''.", "ex_ko": "기존의 접근 방식은 플라즈마의 밀도를 먼저 높인 뒤 열을 공급하는 순서를 따랐습니다.", "ex_en": "The conventional approach followed the order of first raising plasma density and then supplying heat."}, {"name": "~기 전에", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Temporal preposition meaning ''before.'' The ~기 nominalizer + 전에 indicates that action 1 occurs before action 2.", "ex_ko": "그러나 연구진의 계산에 의하면, 순서를 반대로 하여 밀도를 높이기 전에 플라즈마를 먼저 가열하는 방법이 훨씬 효율적일 수 있다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "However, according to the team''s calculations, reversing the order and heating the plasma first, before raising its density, could be far more efficient."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다고 하다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Reports a claim of possibility: 효율적이다 → 효율적일 수 있다고 합니다 ''(they say it) could be efficient''.", "ex_ko": "그러나 연구진의 계산에 의하면, 순서를 반대로 하여 밀도를 높이기 전에 플라즈마를 먼저 가열하는 방법이 훨씬 효율적일 수 있다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "However, according to the team''s calculations, reversing the order and heating the plasma first, before raising its density, could be far more efficient."}, {"name": "~(으)려는", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "''Trying / intending to'' as a noun modifier: 넘다 → 넘으려는 것 ''an attempt to cross (head-on)''.", "ex_ko": "기존 방식이 산 정상을 정면으로 넘으려는 것이라면, 새로운 방식은 더 낮은 고개를 통해 우회하는 것과 같다고 하였습니다.", "ex_en": "If the conventional method is like trying to climb straight over a mountain peak, the new method is like going around it through a lower pass, he said."}, {"name": "~(이)라면", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "''If it is…'' after a noun: 것이다 → 것이라면 ''if (the old way) is…''.", "ex_ko": "기존 방식이 산 정상을 정면으로 넘으려는 것이라면, 새로운 방식은 더 낮은 고개를 통해 우회하는 것과 같다고 하였습니다.", "ex_en": "If the conventional method is like trying to climb straight over a mountain peak, the new method is like going around it through a lower pass, he said."}, {"name": "~는 것과 같다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Simile or comparison construction. Nominalizer ~는 것 + comparison marker 와/과 + 같다 (same/like).", "ex_ko": "기존 방식이 산 정상을 정면으로 넘으려는 것이라면, 새로운 방식은 더 낮은 고개를 통해 우회하는 것과 같다고 하였습니다.", "ex_en": "If the conventional method is like trying to climb straight over a mountain peak, the new method is like going around it through a lower pass, he said."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mv2wewmfsprr' and md5(translation) = '70660e53bb1f9cbfd8c488f498739968';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There is a bear named Odum in India. He was rescued from bad people a long time ago.", "In 2009, actress Julia Roberts came to India. At that time, she saw the bear and gave him the name ''Odum.''", "Odum is now 26 years old. He lives at an animal rescue center in India, where he eats melon and plays in a pool.", "An animal rescue organization said they will keep taking good care of Odum even as he gets older."], "sentences": [{"text": "인도에 오둠이라는 곰이 있어요.", "translation": "In India, there is a bear named Oodum.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인도", "en": "India"}, {"ko": "곰", "en": "bear"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to be"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이라는", "exp": "Quotative particle indicating a name or label. Attaches to noun (이름) to mean ''called/named ~''.", "example_in_sentence": "오둠이라는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. Base form 있다 → 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 곰은 오래전에 나쁜 사람들에게서 구조됐어요.", "translation": "This bear was rescued from bad people a long time ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오래전", "en": "long ago"}, {"ko": "나쁘다", "en": "to be bad"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people"}, {"ko": "구조하다", "en": "to rescue; to save"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게서", "exp": "Postposition marking source of action. Indicates from whom/what an action originates.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들에게서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. Base form 구조되다 → 구조됐어요.", "example_in_sentence": "구조됐어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "피동형 (수동태)", "exp": "Passive voice: 구조하다 (to rescue) → 구조되다 (to be rescued).", "example_in_sentence": "구조됐어요"}]}, {"text": "2009년에 배우 줄리아 로버츠가 인도에 왔어요.", "translation": "In 2009, actress Julia Roberts came to India.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배우", "en": "actor; actress"}, {"ko": "오다", "en": "to come"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Postposition marking time point or location. Here: time (2009년에).", "example_in_sentence": "2009년에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. Base form 오다 → 왔어요.", "example_in_sentence": "왔어요"}]}, {"text": "그때 그녀는 곰을 보고 ''오둠''이라는 이름을 지어 줬어요.", "translation": "Then she saw the bear and gave it the name ''Oodum''.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그때", "en": "at that time; then"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see"}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name"}, {"ko": "짓다", "en": "to make; to give (a name)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Conjunction linking two sequential actions. Base: 보다 → 보고 (and then).", "example_in_sentence": "보고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object particle. After a consonant use 을: 곰을 ''the bear'', 이름을 ''a name''.", "example_in_sentence": "곰을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 주다", "exp": "Auxiliary verb meaning ''to do (for someone)''. Base: 짓다 → 지어 주다 → 지어 줬어요.", "example_in_sentence": "지어 줬어요"}]}, {"text": "오둠은 지금 26살이에요.", "translation": "Oodum is now 26 years old.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금", "en": "now"}, {"ko": "살", "en": "years old"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Copula (to be) + polite ending. For nouns ending in consonant (26살이에요).", "example_in_sentence": "살이에요"}]}, {"text": "인도의 한 동물 보호 센터에서 살아요.", "translation": "He lives in an animal protection center in India.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}, {"ko": "보호", "en": "protection"}, {"ko": "센터", "en": "center"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle marking attribution or relation. Noun + 의 + noun.", "example_in_sentence": "인도의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Postposition marking location where an action occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "센터에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. Base form 살다 → 살아요.", "example_in_sentence": "살아요"}]}, {"text": "멜론도 먹고, 수영장에서 놀기도 해요.", "translation": "He eats melon too, and also plays in a swimming pool.", "vocab": [{"ko": "멜론", "en": "melon"}, {"ko": "먹다", "en": "to eat"}, {"ko": "수영장", "en": "swimming pool"}, {"ko": "놀다", "en": "to play"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also; too'': 멜론 + 도 = ''melon too''.", "example_in_sentence": "멜론도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Conjunction linking coordinate clauses. Base: 먹다 → 먹고.", "example_in_sentence": "먹고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기도 하다", "exp": "''Also does…'': 놀다 → 놀기도 해요 ''(he) also plays''.", "example_in_sentence": "놀기도 해요"}]}, {"text": "동물 구조 단체는 말했어요.", "translation": "The animal rescue group said this:", "vocab": [{"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}, {"ko": "구조", "en": "rescue"}, {"ko": "단체", "en": "organization; group"}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say; to speak"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. Base form 말하다 → 말했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "말했어요"}]}, {"text": "오둠이 나이가 들어도 계속 잘 돌봐 줄 거라고요.", "translation": "They said they will continue to take good care of Oodum even as he gets older.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나이", "en": "age"}, {"ko": "나이가 들다", "en": "to get older"}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; keep (doing)"}, {"ko": "돌보다", "en": "to care for; to look after"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~어도", "exp": "Concessive connector meaning ''even if; even though''. Base: 들다 → 들어도.", "example_in_sentence": "들어도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 주다", "exp": "Auxiliary verb ''to do for someone''. Base: 돌보다 → 돌봐 주다.", "example_in_sentence": "돌봐 줄"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 거예요", "exp": "Future / intention ''will'': 주다 → 줄 거예요 ''will (take care)''. Inside the quote it becomes 줄 거라고요.", "example_in_sentence": "줄 거라고요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고요", "exp": "Ends a sentence that reports what someone said: ''…, they said.'' 줄 거예요 → 줄 거라고요.", "example_in_sentence": "거라고요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "인도", "en": "India", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곰", "en": "bear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to be", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오래전", "en": "long ago", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나쁘다", "en": "to be bad", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구조하다", "en": "to rescue; to save", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배우", "en": "actor; actress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오다", "en": "to come", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그때", "en": "at that time; then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "짓다", "en": "to make; to give (a name)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살", "en": "years old", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보호", "en": "protection", "note": ""}, {"ko": "센터", "en": "center", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "멜론", "en": "melon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "먹다", "en": "to eat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수영장", "en": "swimming pool", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀다", "en": "to play", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구조", "en": "rescue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단체", "en": "organization; group", "note": ""}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say; to speak", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나이", "en": "age", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나이가 들다", "en": "to get older", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; keep (doing)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돌보다", "en": "to care for; to look after", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~이라는", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Quotative particle indicating a name or label. Attaches to noun (이름) to mean ''called/named ~''.", "ex_ko": "인도에 오둠이라는 곰이 있어요.", "ex_en": "In India, there is a bear named Oodum."}, {"name": "~어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. Base form 있다 → 있어요.", "ex_ko": "인도에 오둠이라는 곰이 있어요.", "ex_en": "In India, there is a bear named Oodum."}, {"name": "~에게서", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Postposition marking source of action. Indicates from whom/what an action originates.", "ex_ko": "이 곰은 오래전에 나쁜 사람들에게서 구조됐어요.", "ex_en": "This bear was rescued from bad people a long time ago."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. Base form 구조되다 → 구조됐어요.", "ex_ko": "이 곰은 오래전에 나쁜 사람들에게서 구조됐어요.", "ex_en": "This bear was rescued from bad people a long time ago."}, {"name": "피동형 (수동태)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Passive voice: 구조하다 (to rescue) → 구조되다 (to be rescued).", "ex_ko": "이 곰은 오래전에 나쁜 사람들에게서 구조됐어요.", "ex_en": "This bear was rescued from bad people a long time ago."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Postposition marking time point or location. Here: time (2009년에).", "ex_ko": "2009년에 배우 줄리아 로버츠가 인도에 왔어요.", "ex_en": "In 2009, actress Julia Roberts came to India."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Conjunction linking two sequential actions. Base: 보다 → 보고 (and then).", "ex_ko": "그때 그녀는 곰을 보고 ''오둠''이라는 이름을 지어 줬어요.", "ex_en": "Then she saw the bear and gave it the name ''Oodum''."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Object particle. After a consonant use 을: 곰을 ''the bear'', 이름을 ''a name''.", "ex_ko": "그때 그녀는 곰을 보고 ''오둠''이라는 이름을 지어 줬어요.", "ex_en": "Then she saw the bear and gave it the name ''Oodum''."}, {"name": "~아/어 주다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Auxiliary verb meaning ''to do (for someone)''. Base: 짓다 → 지어 주다 → 지어 줬어요.", "ex_ko": "그때 그녀는 곰을 보고 ''오둠''이라는 이름을 지어 줬어요.", "ex_en": "Then she saw the bear and gave it the name ''Oodum''."}, {"name": "~이에요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Copula (to be) + polite ending. For nouns ending in consonant (26살이에요).", "ex_ko": "오둠은 지금 26살이에요.", "ex_en": "Oodum is now 26 years old."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Possessive particle marking attribution or relation. Noun + 의 + noun.", "ex_ko": "인도의 한 동물 보호 센터에서 살아요.", "ex_en": "He lives in an animal protection center in India."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also; too'': 멜론 + 도 = ''melon too''.", "ex_ko": "멜론도 먹고, 수영장에서 놀기도 해요.", "ex_en": "He eats melon too, and also plays in a swimming pool."}, {"name": "~기도 하다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "''Also does…'': 놀다 → 놀기도 해요 ''(he) also plays''.", "ex_ko": "멜론도 먹고, 수영장에서 놀기도 해요.", "ex_en": "He eats melon too, and also plays in a swimming pool."}, {"name": "~어도", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Concessive connector meaning ''even if; even though''. Base: 들다 → 들어도.", "ex_ko": "오둠이 나이가 들어도 계속 잘 돌봐 줄 거라고요.", "ex_en": "They said they will continue to take good care of Oodum even as he gets older."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 거예요", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Future / intention ''will'': 주다 → 줄 거예요 ''will (take care)''. Inside the quote it becomes 줄 거라고요.", "ex_ko": "오둠이 나이가 들어도 계속 잘 돌봐 줄 거라고요.", "ex_en": "They said they will continue to take good care of Oodum even as he gets older."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mv3t4j0lrg4n' and md5(translation) = 'fa65bd597315a2e75679d48c60e4645b';
